<category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><category term="role:bankruptcy"/><published>2026-07-05T09:21:56.042724+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/change-judge-carys-2026-hearing-dates#e2ae52cb3d2f07fe</id><title>Change to Judge Cary's 2026 Hearing Dates</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:02:11.063214+00:00</updated><link href="https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/change-judge-carys-2026-hearing-dates"/><category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><published>2026-07-05T09:21:56.042724+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/announcement-bankruptcy-judgeship-vacancy-district-massachusetts#00de66a309000e77</id><title>Announcement - Bankruptcy Judgeship Vacancy, District of Massachusetts</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:02:11.063187+00:00</updated><link href="https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/announcement-bankruptcy-judgeship-vacancy-district-massachusetts"/><category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><category term="role:bankruptcy"/><published>2026-07-05T09:21:56.042724+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/multiple-appointments-panel-chapter-7-trustees#9f1fb58a0ce06ae4</id><title>MULTIPLE APPOINTMENTS TO PANEL OF CHAPTER 7 TRUSTEES</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:02:11.063145+00:00</updated><link href="https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/multiple-appointments-panel-chapter-7-trustees"/><category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><category term="role:bankruptcy"/><published>2026-07-05T09:21:56.042724+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/pacer-temporary-fee-increase-effective-jan-1-2027#717b6397a11ea7ce</id><title>Pacer - Temporary Fee Increase Effective Jan. 1, 2027</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:02:11.063112+00:00</updated><content type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<div class="node__content">
<div class="field field--name-field-news-date field--type-date field--label-hidden"><div class="field__items"><div class="field__item even"><span class="date-display-single" content="2026-09-02T00:00:00-04:00" datatype="xsd:dateTime" property="dc:date">Wednesday, September 2, 2026</span></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden"><div class="field__items"><div class="field__item even" property="content:encoded"><p>On Jan. 1, 2027, a temporary increase in fees for electronic access to court records will take effect to help reimburse the costs of the development of the new case management and public access system. </p>
<p>The increase of two cents per page, from 10 cents to 12 cents, was approved by the Judicial Conference’s Executive Committee on behalf of the Judicial Conference of the United States. In addition, the automatic exemption for PACER fees was raised from $30 to $40 per quarter, ensuring that most individual users (those who use $40 or less in PACER services per quarter) would continue to incur no fee or fee increase.</p>
<p>The fee increase will remain in place for a five-year period.</p>
<p>Related links:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href="https://www.uscourts.gov/data-news/judiciary-news/2026/06/26/judiciary-approves-funding-case-management-and-public-access-modernization">Judiciary Approves Funding for Case Management Modernization</a></li>
<li><a href="https://www.uscourts.gov/data-news/judiciary-news/2026/03/10/judges-outline-accelerated-modernization-case-management-system">Judges Outline Accelerated Modernization of Case Management System</a></li>
</ul>
</div></div></div> </div>]]></content><link href="https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/pacer-temporary-fee-increase-effective-jan-1-2027"/><category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><category term="role:estate-probate"/><published>2026-09-02T16:33:30.109701+00:00</published></entry><entry><id>https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/bnc-notice-service-disruption#755e9f7c597e496e</id><title>BNC Notice &amp; Service Disruption</title><updated>2026-10-15T17:02:11.063062+00:00</updated><content type="CDATA"><![CDATA[<div class="node__content">
<div class="field field--name-field-news-date field--type-date field--label-hidden"><div class="field__items"><div class="field__item even"><span class="date-display-single" content="2026-10-15T00:00:00-04:00" datatype="xsd:dateTime" property="dc:date">Thursday, October 15, 2026</span></div></div></div><div class="field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden"><div class="field__items"><div class="field__item even" property="content:encoded"><p>The Bankruptcy Noticing Center (BNC) has been experiencing a nationwide service disruption since on or about October 9, 2026, affecting all U.S. Bankruptcy Courts. The outage has interrupted the BNC's processing and delivery of notices and orders issued by the Court. As a result, parties who ordinarily receive notices and orders through the BNC may experience delays in receiving those documents. The outage is also affecting CM/ECF users' ability to generate and print a List of Creditors.</p>
<p>The outage does not affect the electronic delivery of Notices of Electronic Filing (NEFs), which continue to be generated and distributed normally through CM/ECF.</p>
<p>At this time, there is no estimated date or time for restoration of services. </p>
<p>Additionally, the following websites are unavailable:</p>
<ul>
<li>bnc.uscourts.gov</li>
<li>bankruptcynotices.uscourts.gov</li>
<li>notices.uscourts.gov</li>
<li>National Creditor Registration Service website that supports CM/ECF access to address labels</li>
</ul>
<p>The Court will provide additional updates as information becomes available.</p>
</div></div></div> </div>]]></content><link href="https://www.meb.uscourts.gov/news/bnc-notice-service-disruption"/><category term="Federal Maine-Related"/><category term="Bankruptcy Court notices"/><published>2026-10-15T17:02:08.911878+00:00</published></entry></feed>